# Who owns the edge of each range. One row per answer, with how many claims gave it.
#
# The pair with narrowsWhen is the point
#   One says what would make a range smaller, the other says who owns the edge it would have to
#   move. A negotiated bound moves by renegotiating; a bound that is simply where the measurements
#   fell moves by measuring again; an intrinsic one does not move at all. Same width, three
#   different courses of action, and only one of them is a purchase order.
#
# What a required, typed answer shows
#   As an optional bare enumeration this was almost never filed. Required and typed, two answers
#   stand out that the single column could not have produced: `none`, where nothing sets the edge
#   and the range is simply where the measurements fell, and `derived`, where the model already
#   states the author in a sibling element and had no way to point at it. Which of the two leads
#   moves with the corpus, so prefer the shape of the answer to its rank; run this report for the
#   order.
-- pm:Claim/pm:boundOrigin, over the corpus.
SELECT e.who_owns_the_edge, count(*) AS claims
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/edges.sqlc)
) e
JOIN (
    :compose(scope/corpus.sqlc)
) s USING (filing)
GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 2 DESC
